        "A worked plan turns an idea into a build: write the input, output and three example cases first; sketch the functions; build the smallest version that runs end to end on one case; then add validation, then the remaining cases, testing each addition. Programs built this way are running on day one and grow by accretion, not by a giant-bang finish.",
